      "message": {
        "content": "\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R117/2007-NL1-16.01\",\n    \"project_number\": \"1900647\",\n    \"page_total\": 3,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2017-10-03\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\n      \"Hugo de Grootplein 1\",\n      \"3314 EG Dordrecht\",\n      \"the Netherlands\"\n    ],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"C. Oosterman\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Head Certification Board\",\n    \"phone\": \"+31 78 6332332\",\n    \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n    \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Tokheim Sofitam Applications S.A.S part of Dover Fueling Solutions\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\n        \"Immeuble Le Cézanne\",\n        \"Paris Nord, 31 - 35 Allée des Impressionnistes\",\n        \"BP 45027 Villepinte\",\n        \"95912 Roissy Ch de Gaulle Cedex\",\n        \"France\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Tokheim Sofitam Applications S.A.S part of Dover Fueling Solutions\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\n        \"Immeuble Le Cézanne\",\n        \"Paris Nord, 31 - 35 Allée des Impressionnistes\",\n        \"BP 45027 Villepinte\",\n        \"95912 Roissy Ch de Gaulle Cedex\",\n        \"France\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Fuel dispenser\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"Quantium XXXX\"],\n    \"description\": \"Fuel dispenser comprising one or more measuring systems in the same housing. Each measuring system consists of one Tokheim combined pump and gas elimination device (TQP-RS (EPZ with a high cover), EPZ with a lower top cover, TK80, or TQP-HS (PAS V3)), one Tokheim TQM measurement transducer, and one Tokheim WWC v4, WWV v7 or TQCL-C calculating/indicating device. One Tokheim combined pump and gas eliminator can be connected with two measurement transducers, each measurement transducer being considered as part of a measuring system. When more than one measuring system is in one housing, the calculating/indicating device may be a common part of the measuring systems. A Qmax of 130 L/min can be reached by connecting two gas separators (or one gas separator if the Qmax is sufficient) and two measurement transducers in parallel with delivery via one hose with nozzle. For multi-product dispensers it is only possible to deliver one product at the same time on one side of the dispenser. The construction of the measuring instrument is recorded in Documentation folder no. T10001-7.\"\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"combined pump and gas elimination device\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"EPZ\", \"TQP-RS\", \"TK80\", \"TQP-HS (PAS V3)\"],\n      \"alternatives\": \"OR\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"measurement transducer\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"TQM\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"calculating/indicating device\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"WWC v4\", \"WWV v7\", \"TQCL-C\", \"TQCL\"],\n      \"alternatives\": \"OR\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"accuracy_class\": {\n        \"value\": 0.5,\n        \"unit_symbol\": null,\n        \"unit_id\": null\n      },\n      \"minimum_flowrate\": {\n        \"value\": 2.0,\n        \"unit_symbol\": \"L/min\",\n        \"unit_id\": null\n      },\n      \"minimum_measured_quantity\": {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"unit_symbol\": \"L\",\n        \"unit_id\": null\n      },\n      \"liquid_product\": {\n        \"value\": \"gasoline/gasoil\",\n        \"unit_symbol\": null,\n        \"unit_id\": null\n      },\n      \"maximum_volume_indication\": {\n        \"value\": 9999.99,\n        \"unit_symbol\": \"L\",\n        \"unit_id\": null,\n        \"footnote_markers\": [\"*)\"]\n      },\n      \"maximum_unit_price\": {\n        \"value\": 9.999,\n        \"unit_symbol\": \"€/L\",\n        \"unit_id\": null,\n        \"footnote_markers\": [\"*)\", \"**)\"]\n      },\n      \"maximum_price_to_pay\": {\n        \"value\": 9999.99,\n        \"unit_symbol\": \"€\",\n        \"unit_id\": null,\n        \"footnote_markers\": [\"*)\", \"**)\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"maximum_flowrate\",\n        \"axis\": \"pump_configuration\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"standard configuration\",\n            \"value\": 80,\n            \"unit_symbol\": \"L/min\",\n            \"unit_id\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"two gas separators and two measurement transducers in parallel with delivery via one hose with nozzle\",\n            \"value\": 130,\n            \"unit_symbol\": \"L/min\",\n            \"unit_id\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"General characteristics of the measuring instrument\",\n      \"columns\": [\n        \"maximum_flowrate\",\n        \"minimum_flowrate\",\n        \"accuracy_class\",\n        \"minimum_measured_quantity\",\n        \"liquid_product\",\n        \"maximum_volume_indication\",\n        \"maximum_unit_price\",\n        \"maximum_price_to_pay\"\n      ],\n      \"column_units\": [\"L/min\", \"L/min\", null, \"L\", null, \"L\", \"€/L\", \"€\"],\n      \"rows\": [\n        {\n          \"maximum_flowrate\": 80,\n          \"minimum_flowrate\": 2.0,\n          \"accuracy_class\": 0.5,\n          \"minimum_measured_quantity\": 2,\n          \"liquid_product\": \"gasoline/gasoil\",\n          \"maximum_volume_indication\": 9999.99,\n          \"maximum_unit_price\": 9.999,\n          \"maximum_price_to_pay\": 9999.99\n        },\n        {\n          \"maximum_flowrate\": 130,\n          \"minimum_flowrate\": 2.0,\n          \"accuracy_class\": 0.5,\n          \"minimum_measured_quantity\": 2,\n          \"liquid_product\": \"gasoline/gasoil\",\n          \"maximum_volume_indication\": 9999.99,\n          \"maximum_unit_price\": 9.999,\n          \"maximum_price_to_pay\": 9999.99\n        }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"General characteristics per configuration row. The 130 L/min maximum flowrate is reached by connecting two gas separators and two measurement transducers in parallel with delivery via one hose with nozzle.\",\n      \"footnotes\": [\"*)\", \"**)\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R117-1\",\n    \"edition\": 2007,\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [\"0.5\"]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CPC-810762-01\",\n      \"date\": \"2009-03-30\",\n      \"pages\": 17,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CPC-702138\",\n      \"date\": \"2007-09-12\",\n      \"pages\": 19,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CPC-702138-1\",\n      \"date\": \"2007-09-21\",\n      \"pages\": 23,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NMO Evaluation Report No. P00882 TK80 Gas Separator\",\n      \"date\": \"2012-07-09\",\n      \"role\": \"evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"OIML Test Report No. SN 1221\",\n      \"date\": \"2012-07-09\",\n      \"pages\": 12,\n      \"role\": \"test_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R117/1995-NL1-01.04\",\n      \"date\": \"2004-01-21\",\n      \"pages\": 36,\n      \"role\": \"evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CPC/608514\",\n      \"date\": \"2007-02-14\",\n      \"pages\": 76,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CPC/705081\",\n      \"date\": \"2007-07-18\",\n      \"pages\": 64,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CPC/507848\",\n      \"date\": \"2006-05-19\",\n      \"pages\": 72,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P147764\",\n      \"date\": \"2015-11-18\",\n      \"pages\": 26,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P135196\",\n      \"date\": \"2015-04-10\",\n      \"pages\": 30,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T10001-7\",\n      \"role\": \"documentation_file\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\n      \"revision\": \"Initial\",\n      \"date\": \"2016-07-07\",\n      \"changes\": \"Quantium XXXX Fuel Dispenser\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"revision\": \"1\",\n      \"date\": \"2017-10-03\",\n      \"changes\": \"Correction typing error in documentation folder number and extension of the manufacturers name with part of Dover Fueling Solutions\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"footnotes\": [\n    {\n      \"marker\": \"*)\",\n      \"text\": \"The decimal sign can be shown on different positions in the LCD-Display(s)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"marker\": \"**)\".replace(\"\\\"\", \"\"),\n      \"text\": \"The currency is depends on the applicable country (Nationality)\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n",
        "reasoning_content": "Let me analyze this OIML Certificate of Conformity.\n\nKey fields:\n- Certificate number: R117/2007-NL1-16.01 revision 1\n- Project number: 1900647\n- Page total: 3\n- Member state: The Netherlands\n- Date issued: 3 October 2017\n- OIML issuer id: NL1 (NMi Certin B.V., OIML Issuing Authority NL1)\n- Issuing authority: NMi Certin B.V., address: Hugo de Grootplein 1, 3314 EG Dordrecht, the Netherlands; person responsible: C. Oosterman; title: Head Certification Board; phone: +31 78 6332332; email: certin@nmi.nl; website: www.nmi.nl\n- Applicant and Manufacturer: Tokheim Sofitam Applications S.A.S part of Dover Fueling Solutions, address lines: Immeuble Le Cézanne, Paris Nord, 31 - 35 Allée des Impressionnistes, BP 45027 Villepinte, 95912 Roissy Ch de Gaulle Cedex, France\n- Certified type: fuel dispenser, type: Quantium XXXX\n- Recommendation: R117-1 (2007) — canonical id \"R117-1\"? The rule says canonical e.g. \"R60\". This is R117-1, edition 2007. Accuracy class 0.5.\n- Scheme: OIML Certificate of Conformity — scheme... The certificate \"scheme\" field in certificate: scheme (A|B). Hmm, for OIML-CS, scheme A or B. This certificate is issued under the OIML Basic Certificate System... Not explicitly stated. NMi certs from 2017 - the OIML Certificate System. Not stated which scheme. I'll omit or set null. Actually the schema says scheme (A|B) for certificate. Since it's not stated, omit.\n\nTest reports:\n- CPC-810762-01 dated 30 March 2009, 17 pages — for Quantium XXXX including TQM Measurement Transducer, EPZ, TQP-RS or TK80 gas elimination device and WWC v4 or calculating/indicating device. Role: type_evaluation_report? It's \"report(s)\". These are Type Evaluation Reports / test reports. Let me assign roles:\n  - CPC-810762-01: type_evaluation_report\n  - CPC-702138 (12 Sept 2007, 19 pages) for TQM Measurement Transducer\n  - CPC-702138-1 (21 Sept 2007, 23 pages) for EPZ or TQP-RS gas elimination device\n  - NMO Evaluation Report No. P00882 TK80 Gas Separator and OIML Test Report No. SN 1221 dated 9 July 2012, 12 pages — this is two reports? \"NMO Evaluation Report No. P00882 TK80 Gas Separator and OIML Test Report No. SN 1221 dated 9 July 2012 that includes 12 pages.\" Could be listed as two entries or one. I'll list as two test reports: P00882 (evaluation_report) and SN 1221 (test_report), both dated 9 July 2012, 12 pages. Hmm, \"that includes 12 pages\" refers to the combined. Safer to list both with same date/pages, or one entry with id \"NMO Evaluation Report No. P00882 TK80 Gas Separator and OIML Test Report No. SN 1221\". I'll make two entries with a note. Actually the schema test_reports[] has id, date, pages, role. I'll do two entries.\n  - R117/1995-NL1-01.04 dated 21 January 2004, 36 pages — for TQP-HS (PAS V3) gas elimination device. Note: this looks like a certificate number actually, but it's listed as report. Role: evaluation_report? I'll use type_evaluation_report or documentation. Hmm. I'll keep as listed; role \"evaluation_report\".\n  - CPC/608514 dated 14 February 2007, 76 pages — for WWC v4 calculating/indicating device\n  - CPC/705081 dated 18 July 2007, 64 pages — for WWC v4\n  - CPC/507848 dated 19 May 2006, 72 pages — for WWV v7\n  - CPC/608514 (same as above, also for WWV v7)\n  - CPC/705081 (same, also for WWV v7)\n  - P147764 dated 18 November 2015, 26 pages — TQCL-C\n  - P135196 dated 10 April 2015, 30 pages — TQCL\n\nTest reports list — avoid duplicating CPC/608514 and CPC/705081? They appear under both WWC v4 and WWV v7. I'll list once each but note. Schema doesn't allow annotations. I'll list unique reports once. Actually duplicating might be OK but I'll dedupe: CPC/608514 and CPC/705081 appear twice. I'll include once.\n\nDates format: ISO? \"30 March 2009\" → \"2009-03-30\". I'll use ISO dates.\n\nRevision history:\n- Initial, 7 July 2016, \"Quantium XXXX Fuel Dispenser\"\n- 1, 3 October 2017, \"Correction typing error in documentation folder number and extension of the manufacturers name with part of Dover Fueling Solutions\"\n\nCharacteristics table (page 2): Two rows — two configurations distinguished by max flowrate:\nRow 1: Qmax 80 L/min, Qmin 2.0 L/min, class 0.5, minimum measured quantity 2 L, liquid product gasoline/gasoil, max volume indication 9999.99 L (*), max unit price 9.999 €/L (*), max price to pay 9999.99 € (*)\nRow 2: Qmax 130 L/min, Qmin 2.0 L/min, class 0.5, min measured quantity 2 L, gasoline/gasoil, max volume 9999.99 L, max unit price 9.999 €/L, max price to pay 9999.99 €\n\nThis is a configuration axis: Qmax = 80 L/min vs 130 L/min. The 130 L/min variant is reached by connecting two gas separators and two measurement transducers in parallel. So this is a config-level characteristic. I'll use config_level with axis \"flowrate_configuration\" or similar.\n\nActually per rule 4, this could be a model family of two variants: Quantium XXXX with Qmax 80 vs 130. But it's the same type Quantium XXXX with different configurations. Rule 5 says configuration axes — e.g., static vs dynamic. Here two configurations: single pump (80 L/min) vs dual pump parallel (130 L/min). I'll use config_level.\n\nDecimal fixes: \"2,0\" → 2.0, \"0,5\" → 0.5, \"9999,99\" → 9999.99, \"9,999\" → 9.999.\n\nFootnotes: *) and **) — markers \"*\" and \"**\"? The markdown shows `*)` and `**)`. I'll record markers as \"*)\" and \"**)\". \n\nFootnote texts:\n- *): \"The decimal sign can be shown on different positions in the LCD-Display(s);\"\n- **): \"The currency is depends on the applicable country (Nationality).\"\n\nComponents:\n- \"TQM\" Measurement Transducer — role: measurement transducer\n- Gas elimination device: \"EPZ\", \"TQP-RS\", \"TK80\", \"TQP-HS (PAS V3)\" — alternatives OR. Actually page 3: \"One Tokheim, 'TQP-RS' (EPZ with a high cover) combined pump and gas elimination device, or; One Tokheim, 'TQP-RS' (EPZ with a lower top cover) combined pump and gas elimination device; One Tokheim, 'TK80'...; One Tokheim, 'TQP-HS (PAS V3)'...\" Hmm, the text lists TQP-RS twice — likely a typo: \"TQP-RS (EPZ with a high cover)\" or \"EPZ (with a lower top cover)\"? Actually EPZ is the base; TQP-RS is EPZ with high cover. The second bullet probably should be \"EPZ\" (with a lower top cover). I'll record as given: type_designations: [\"TQP-RS (EPZ with a high cover)\", \"TQP-RS (EPZ with a lower top cover)\", \"TK80\", \"TQP-HS (PAS V3)\"] — but also EPZ mentioned on page 2. Components list: I'll create:\n  - role \"combined pump and gas elimination device\", type_designations: [\"EPZ\", \"TQP-RS\", \"TK80\", \"TQP-HS (PAS V3)\"], alternatives \"OR\", with note about EPZ with high cover = TQP-RS, lower top cover.\n  - role \"measurement transducer\", type_designations: [\"TQM\"]\n  - role \"calculating/indicating device\", type_designations: [\"WWC v4\", \"WWV v7\", \"TQCL-C\", \"TQCL\"]? Page 3 says \"WWC v4\", \"WWV v7\" or \"TQCL-C\". Page 2 mentions TQCL as well (test report for \"TQCL\" calculating/indicating device). I'll include TQCL too since page 2 lists it. Actually page 3 comprising list only includes WWC v4, WWV v7, TQCL-C. Page 2 has report for TQCL too. I'll include all four, alternatives \"OR\".\n\nCertified type:\n- category: \"Fuel dispenser\"\n- type_designations: [\"Quantium XXXX\"]\n- module_designation: null? Not applicable for fuel dispensers. Omit or \"Not applicable\". I'll omit.\n\nDescription: from page 3 — \"Comprising of one or more measuring systems in the same housing. Each measuring system consists of...\" I can put a summary in description.\n\nRecommendation:\n- id: \"R117-1\"? Canonical: \"R117\". The recommendation is \"R117-1 (2007) Dynamic measuring systems for liquids other than water\". Hmm. R117 has parts. The certificate says R117-1. Canonical id: \"R117-1\"? The rule says canonical e.g. \"R60\" not \"OIML R 60\". For part-specific, \"R117-1\" seems fine. Edition: 2007. Accuracy classes: [\"0.5\"]. Scheme: not stated — omit.\n\ncertificate.scheme: not stated. Omit.\n\nmodel_family: only if cert covers >1 model variant. The two rows are configurations of the same model (flowrate). I'll not create model_family; use config_level. Actually could argue two variants. I'll use config_level with axis \"pump_configuration\" with conditions \"Qmax 80 L/min (single pump)\" and \"Qmax 130 L/min (two pumps in parallel)\". Hmm, but the table distinguishes only by Qmax. Let me define axis as \"maximum_flowrate\" with conditions \"80 L/min\" and \"130 L/min\"? Or axis \"configuration\". I'll do:\n\nconfig_level entries:\n- attribute \"maximum_flowrate\", axis \"pump_configuration\", values: [{condition: \"single measurement transducer / standard configuration\", value 80, unit L/min}, {condition: \"two gas separators and two measurement transducers in parallel\", value 130, unit L/min}]\n\nHmm, that inverts — the condition should describe the config and value the attribute. Actually the Qmax is the varying thing; other attributes are same. Simpler: axis = \"Qmax configuration\". Conditions: \"Qmax = 80 L/min\" and \"Qmax = 130 L/min\". Then for other attributes both conditions same value. That's redundant but preserves the table.\n\nAlternatively use matrix_tables to preserve the table as-is, and put config_level for the varying attributes. The schema allows matrix_tables. I'll do both:\n\nmatrix_tables:\n- name \"General characteristics of the measuring instrument\"\n- columns: [\"maximum_flowrate\", \"minimum_flowrate\", \"accuracy_class\", \"minimum_measured_quantity\", \"liquid_product\", \"maximum_volume_indication\", \"maximum_unit_price\", \"maximum_price_to_pay\"]\n- column_units: [\"L/min\", \"L/min\", null, \"L\", null, \"L\", \"€/L\", \"€\"]\n- rows: two rows with numeric values, footnote_markers on the * values.\n- description: general characteristics table; max flowrate 130 achieved by two gas separators and two transducers in parallel.\n- footnotes: markers.\n\ncharacteristics.config_level:\n- attribute \"maximum_flowrate\", axis \"configuration\", values: [{condition: \"single measuring system\", value: 80, unit_symbol: \"L/min\"}, {condition: \"two gas separators and two measurement transducers in parallel\", value: 130, unit_symbol: \"L/min\"}]\n- attribute \"minimum_flowrate\", axis \"configuration\", values: both 2.0 L/min\n- attribute \"minimum_measured_quantity\", both 2 L\n- attribute \"maximum_volume_indication\", both 9999.99 L with footnote \"*\"\n- attribute \"maximum_unit_price\", both 9.999 €/L with footnote \"*\"\n- attribute \"maximum_price_to_pay\", both 9999.99 € with footnote \"*\"\n- liquid_product: both \"gasoline/gasoil\" — value string; unit null.\n- accuracy_class: 0.5 — type_level? It's in recommendation. Could include type_level accuracy_class 0.5.\n\ntype_level:\n- accuracy_class: 0.5\n- liquid_product: \"gasoline/gasoil\"? It's same for both configs, so type_level is fine.\n- min measured quantity 2 L also same → could be type_level. But keep config-level for consistency? I'll put invariant ones at type_level: minimum_measured_quantity, minimum_flowrate, liquid_product. And config_level only for maximum_flowrate (the varying one) plus the display ones? The display ones are the same for both too. Hmm.\n\nSimplest clean approach:\n- type_level: minimum_flowrate 2.0 L/min; minimum_measured_quantity 2 L; liquid_product \"gasoline/gasoil\"; maximum_volume_indication 9999.99 L; maximum_unit_price 9.999 €/L; maximum_price_to_pay 9999.99 €; accuracy_class 0.5.\n- config_level: maximum_flowrate with two conditions.\n\nThat seems reasonable and avoids redundancy.\n\nFootnote markers: the table shows *) attached to 9999,99, 9,999, 9999,99 and **) on the headers \"Maximum unit price € / L **)\" and \"Maximum price to pay € **)\". So max_unit_price and max_price_to_pay get marker \"**)\"? Actually the headers have **) and the values have *). Both apply: values have *), columns have **). I'll put footnote_markers [\"*)\", \"**)\"] on max_unit_price and max_price_to_pay values, and [\"*)\"] on max_volume_indication.\n\nWait — the **) on the header: \"Maximum unit price € / L **)\" and \"Maximum price to pay € **)\". Yes.\n\nCertificate number: \"R117/2007-NL1-16.01\" revision 1. number field: \"R117/2007-NL1-16.01\". revision_history captures revision 1 and initial. Should number include \"revision 1\"? I'll keep number as \"R117/2007-NL1-16.01\" and note revision in... certificate schema doesn't have revision field. Hmm, revision_history includes it. Fine.\n\noiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\".\n\ndate_issued: \"2017-10-03\".\n\nissuing_authority:\n- name: \"NMi Certin B.V.\"\n- address_lines: [\"Hugo de Grootplein 1\", \"3314 EG Dordrecht\", \"the Netherlands\"]\n- person_responsible: \"C. Oosterman\"\n- person_title: \"Head Certification Board\"\n- phone: \"+31 78 6332332\"\n- email: \"certin@nmi.nl\"\n- website: \"www.nmi.nl\"\n- oiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\"\n\napplicants: [{name: \"Tokheim Sofitam Applications S.A.S part of Dover Fueling Solutions\", address_lines: [\"Immeuble Le Cézanne\", \"Paris Nord, 31 - 35 Allée des Impressionnistes\", \"BP 45027 Villepinte\", \"95912 Roissy Ch de Gaulle Cedex\", \"France\"]}]\n\nmanufacturers: same (Applicant and Manufacturer).\n\ncertified_type:\n- category: \"Fuel dispenser\"\n- type_designations: [\"Quantium XXXX\"]\n- description: \"Fuel dispenser comprising one or more measuring systems in the same housing; each measuring system consists of a Tokheim combined pump and gas elimination device (TQP-RS / TK80 / TQP-HS (PAS V3)), a TQM measurement transducer, and a WWC v4, WWV v7 or TQCL-C calculating/indicating device. A Qmax of 130 L/min is reached by connecting two gas separators and two measurement transducers in parallel with delivery via one hose with nozzle. For multi-product dispensers only one product can be delivered at a time on one side of the dispenser.\"\n\ntest_reports entries with ids and roles:\n1. CPC-810762-01, 2009-03-30, 17, type_evaluation_report — covers Quantium XXXX including TQM, EPZ, TQP-RS or TK80 gas elimination device and WWC v4 calculating/indicating device.\n2. CPC-702138, 2007-09-12, 19, type_evaluation_report — TQM Measurement Transducer\n3. CPC-702138-1, 2007-09-21, 23, type_evaluation_report — EPZ or TQP-RS gas elimination device\n4. NMO P00882, 2012-07-09, 12, evaluation_report — TK80 Gas Separator\n5. SN 1221, 2012-07-09, 12, test_report — OIML Test Report for TK80\n6. R117/1995-NL1-01.04, 2004-01-21, 36, ... role? It's a report listed for TQP-HS (PAS V3). Could be a certificate actually. I'll call it \"evaluation_report\".\n7. CPC/608514, 2007-02-14, 76, type_evaluation_report — WWC v4 (also WWV v7)\n8. CPC/705081, 2007-07-18, 64, type_evaluation_report — WWC v4 (also WWV v7)\n9. CPC/507848, 2006-05-19, 72, type_evaluation_report — WWV v7\n10. P147764, 2015-11-18, 26, type_evaluation_report — TQCL-C\n11. P135196, 2015-04-10, 30, type_evaluation_report — TQCL\n\nSchema doesn't have a \"applies_to\" field for test reports; role only. Fine — just id, date, pages, role.\n\nrevision_history:\n- {revision: \"Initial\", date: \"2016-07-07\", changes: \"Quantium XXXX Fuel Dispenser\"}\n- {revision: \"1\", date: \"2017-10-03\", changes: \"Correction typing error in documentation folder number and extension of the manufacturers name with part of Dover Fueling Solutions\"}\n\nfootnotes:\n- {marker: \"*)\", text: \"The decimal sign can be shown on different positions in the LCD-Display(s);\"}\n- {marker: \"**)\". text: \"The currency is depends on the applicable country (Nationality).\"}\n\nRecommendation accuracy_classes: [\"0.5\"] — should be number or string? Schema says accuracy_classes[]. I'll use [0.5] as number. Or [\"0.5\"]. Classes like \"0,5\" — I'll use 0.5 number. Hmm, accuracy classes are usually strings like \"0.5\". Either works. I'll use [\"0.5\"].\n\nCertificate scheme field: omit (not stated).\n\npage_total: 3.\n\nNow components details:\n\ncomponents:\n1. {role: \"combined pump and gas elimination device\", type_d